{#
  Shown when a store-only re-render fails.

  The Financials Refresh recomputes the report from .store/raw.duckdb with zero
  network calls. When that render raises (a cleared cache, an unwritable cache,
  a malformed payload) it used to be swallowed: the runner logged a warning and
  returned a stale artifact or nothing, so the tab silently emptied and the app
  went back over the network. This board is written over the artifact so the
  failure is displayed instead of papered over. The data itself is untouched in
  .store — re-running Fetch retries the live path.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<style>
body{background:#0d1117;color:#c9d1d9;font-family:'Segoe UI',Consolas,monospace;padding:40px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}
h1{color:#f85149;font-size:18px;margin-bottom:14px}
.msg{color:#f0f6fc;font-size:14px;margin:14px 0}
.hint{color:#8b949e;font-size:12px}
.stamp{color:#484f58;font-size:11px;margin-top:24px;border-top:1px solid #21262d;padding-top:10px}
details{margin-top:12px}
summary{color:#8b949e;font-size:11px;cursor:pointer}
pre{background:#161b22;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:6px;padding:10px;overflow-x:auto;
    color:#8b949e;font-size:11px;margin-top:8px;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word}
</style></head><body>
<h1>Refresh failed — the report could not be re-rendered from the store</h1>
<div class="msg">{{ message }}</div>
<div class="hint">The stored data was not touched, so no re-fetch should be
needed. If this keeps happening, use the Fetch button to pull fresh data, or
check the server log for the full traceback.</div>
<details>
  <summary>Show the raw error</summary>
  <pre>{{ detail }}</pre>
</details>
<div class="stamp">Generated {{ stamp }}</div>
</body></html>
